<Layout title="Tide pools">
	<p>
		At low tide the sea drains off the rock shelf and leaves pools behind. The anemones pull in
		their tentacles to keep from drying out, then open again when the water comes back over them. On
		summer mornings the fog keeps the pools from warming up too fast.
	</p>
</Layout>
